          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "If the $B-H$ curves of two samples of $X$ and $Y$ of iron are as shown below, then which one of the following statement is correct?\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/Xl4sf4ZM6zttiqfH1nkQGUg60x52xUO4PKZCrxH_A-g.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "wfQ32",
              "text": "\r\nBoth $X$ and $Y$ are suitable for making electromagnets.\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "7WL1R",
              "text": "\r\nBoth $X$ and $Y$ are suitable for making permanent magnet.\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "BjdGT",
              "text": "\r\n$X$ is suitable for making permanent magnet and $Y$ for making electromagnet.\r\n",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "gthtv",
              "text": "\r\n$X$ is suitable for making electromagnet and $Y$ is suitable for permanent magnet.",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "For permanent magnet we prefer a material with high retentivity and high coercivity. For electromagnet, we prefer high saturated magnetism, low coercivity and least possible area of hystersis loop. Therefore, $X$ is suitable for making permanent magnet and $Y$ for making electromagnet.",
            "image": null
          },
